    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3910c982",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two individuals, a man and a woman, posing together at what appears to be an awards ceremony (American Music Awards backdrop). The man is holding an award and wearing a hat and gold chains, while the woman is dressed in a shiny yellow top and patterned pants. The overlaid text reads: 'there's so much white trash in this picture i barely know where to start!'. The meme uses this text to mock the appearance or perceived 'trashiness' of the individuals, particularly targeting their clothing and style. The term 'white trash' is a derogatory stereotype historically used to demean people of lower socioeconomic status, often implying laziness, lack of education, or moral inferiority. This usage is inherently racist and classist, as it relies on a harmful racialized and class-based stereotype to insult the subjects. The intent is to ridicule the subjects' fashion choices and overall presentation, framing them as 'trashy' and unworthy of admiration. This is a form of cyberbullying and harmful content, as it attacks the individuals based on their appearance and social status, potentially causing emotional harm. The meme's overall intent is to provoke laughter through the use of a vulgar, offensive stereotype, thereby normalizing and spreading derogatory language.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7dffa989"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
